<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koressia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Korissia, Arsinoe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koressia was one of the four ancient cities of the island of Keos in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a>, at the main harbour on the north-west coast. In the 3rd century BCE it became a Ptolemaic naval base renamed Arsinoe. The modern port town of Korissia occupies the site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koressia.jpg" alt="Koressia" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Wurdel at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Koriss%C3%ADa_auf_Kea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
